    "result_text": "All tests pass and the build is green. Here's what I did.\n\n## Summary\n\nMoved date-derived values onto a fiscal-year basis (FY starts 1 July, named by the calendar year it ends in \u2014 so 1 July 2025\u201330 June 2026 is FY26).\n\n**New cohesive unit** \u2014 `util/FiscalYears.java`: a small, dependency-free helper with `of(date)`, `yearOfCentury(date)`, `label(date)` (\u2192 `FY<YY>`) and `elapsed(from, to)`. All the fiscal-year arithmetic lives here so the call sites stay one-liners.\n\n**Four minimal edits, each a single expression:**\n- `openapi.yml` \u2014 added the read-only `fiscalYear` field (drives the generated `OwnerDto`) and updated the `membershipNumber` description.\n- `mapper/OwnerMapper.java` \u2014 added the `fiscalYear` mapping and switched `membershipNumber`'s year segment from `getYear() % 100` to `FiscalYears.yearOfCentury(...)`.\n- `rest/.../Tenure.java` \u2014 `exceedsOneYear` now counts elapsed fiscal years (`FiscalYears.elapsed(...) > 1`) instead of a 365-day window.\n- `model/OwnerAuditListener.java` \u2014 the audit-logged membership identifier uses the same fiscal-year segment, keeping the identifier consistent everywhere it's produced.\n\n**Keeping structural impact low:** I didn't grow any existing method or class \u2014 all real logic went into the new tiny `FiscalYears` class (low WMC_other), and every edited function stayed a simple one-expression change. The two duplicated membership-identifier sites and the tenure/label logic all funnel through the shared helper rather than each re-deriving the fiscal year.\n\nThe `fiscalYear` value flows from `owner.getRegistrationDate()`, which is already business-day-adjusted at persist time (`Owner.ensureRegistrationDate` \u2192 `BusinessDays.rollForward`), so it's derived from the business-day-adjusted date as specified.\n\nThe acceptance test (`coreReturnsFiscalYear`, asserting `fiscalYear` matches `FY\\d{2}`) passes, and the audit log confirms the new behaviour (`registrationDate=2026-09-01` \u2192 `membershipNumber=\u2026-M27`, i.e. FY27).",
